<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John VII, Count of Nassau-Siegen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1561–1623</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as John the Middle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John VII, Count of Nassau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siegen">Siegen</a>, known as John the Middle, received Siegen after the death of his father, John VI of Nassau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dillenburg">Dillenburg</a>, in 1606. A leading Calvinist military reformer, he wrote on the drill methods of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> army and founded a military academy at Siegen in 1616. His lands were divided among his sons after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-vii-count-of-nassau-siegen.jpg" alt="John VII, Count of Nassau-Siegen" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Jan van Ravesteyn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jan_de_middelste_van_Nassau-Siegen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
